---
/**
 * Act II, section 07: the bill, and the last thing Act II owes the reader.
 *
 * It closes the act on the question a platform tool is usually least willing to answer, which is
 * why it goes last rather than being folded into the Console section.
 */
import { CostsPanel } from '../../surfaces/CostsPanel';
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
---

<section class="b-band" id="s07" data-act="1">
  <div class="b-shell">
    <SectionHead act="1" index="07" kicker="Console · costs">
      <Fragment slot="title">The bill, with nothing added to it.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="lede">
        The dashboard reads your own Cost Explorer data and breaks the stage down by resource, so "the database is most
        of it" is a thing you can see rather than suspect. AWS invoices you directly. Stacktape does not resell your
        infrastructure and takes no percentage of it.
      </Fragment>
    </SectionHead>

    <figure class="b-figure b-reveal">
      <div class="b-figure__stage site-panel">
        <CostsPanel />
      </div>
      <figcaption class="b-figure__caption">
        <b>Month to date, one stage, six resources.</b> The same breakdown exists per stage, which is how a preview
        environment stops being an unknown.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
